   "source": [
    "# 4. Dataset Loading\n",
    "\n",
    "The PIDGN-T framework integrates three heterogeneous biomedical modalities:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Genomic modality:\n",
    "- SNP profiles representing genetic variations associated with Parkinson's disease.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Neuroimaging modality:\n",
    "- Structural MRI representations extracted from volumetric brain images.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. Clinical and behavioral modality:\n",
    "- Longitudinal clinical observations and behavioral measurements collected across multiple visits.\n",
    "\n",
    "The dataset is organized according to the repository structure:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "data/\n",
    "│\n",
    "├── splits/\n",
    "│   ├── train_split.csv\n",
    "│   ├── validation_split.csv\n",
    "│   └── test_split.csv\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "The split files contain subject-level identifiers and labels used for training, validation, and testing.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# Dataset Path Configuration\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "DATA_PATH = Path('../data/splits/')\n",
    "\n",
    "TRAIN_FILE = DATA_PATH / 'train_split.csv'\n",
    "\n",
    "VALIDATION_FILE = DATA_PATH / 'validation_split.csv'\n",
    "\n",
    "TEST_FILE = DATA_PATH / 'test_split.csv'\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Load Subject-Level Data Splits\n",
    "\n",
    "The following cells load the predefined training, validation, and testing partitions.\n",
    "\n",
    "The subject-level separation strategy prevents information leakage between different experimental phases and follows the evaluation protocol described in the manuscript.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# Load Dataset Splits\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "train_data = pd.read_csv(TRAIN_FILE)\n",
    "\n",
    "validation_data = pd.read_csv(VALIDATION_FILE)\n",
    "\n",
    "test_data = pd.read_csv(TEST_FILE)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Training subjects:', len(train_data))\n",
    "print('Validation subjects:', len(validation_data))\n",
    "print('Testing subjects:', len(test_data))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Dataset Inspection\n",
    "\n",
    "A preliminary inspection is performed to verify the structure of the loaded data.\n",
    "\n",
    "Each record represents one participant and includes:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Subject identifier\n",
    "- Multimodal feature availability\n",
    "- Clinical label\n",
    "- Experimental metadata\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Display first samples\n",
    "\n",
    "train_data.head()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 5. DataLoader Configuration\n",
    "\n",
    "The PyTorch DataLoader provides mini-batch processing during model optimization.\n",
    "\n",
    "The training pipeline uses:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Random shuffling for training batches\n",
    "- Fixed ordering for validation and testing\n",
    "- Configurable batch size according to available hardware resources\n",
    "\n",
    "The actual multimodal dataset implementation is provided in the data preprocessing module.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# DataLoader Configuration\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "BATCH_SIZE = 16\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Placeholder dataset objects\n",
    "# Replace with PIDGN-T multimodal dataset class\n",
    "\n",
    "train_dataset = None\n",
    "\n",
    "validation_dataset = None\n",
    "\n",
    "test_dataset = None\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Dataset objects initialized.')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# Create DataLoaders\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "train_loader = DataLoader(\n",
    "\n",
    "    train_dataset,\n",
    "\n",
    "    batch_size=BATCH_SIZE,\n",
    "\n",
    "    shuffle=True\n",
    "\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "validation_loader = DataLoader(\n",
    "\n",
    "    validation_dataset,\n",
    "\n",
    "    batch_size=BATCH_SIZE,\n",
    "\n",
    "    shuffle=False\n",
    "\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "test_loader = DataLoader(\n",
    "\n",
    "    test_dataset,\n",
    "\n",
    "    batch_size=BATCH_SIZE,\n",
    "\n",
    "    shuffle=False\n",
    "\n",
    ")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 6. PIDGN-T Model Initialization\n",
    "\n",
    "The proposed PIDGN-T architecture integrates multimodal feature extraction, graph learning, temporal reasoning, and explainable prediction.\n",
    "\n",
    "The complete architecture consists of:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Genomic Autoencoder\n",
    "\n",
    "2. 3D MRI Encoder\n",
    "\n",
    "3. Clinical LSTM Encoder\n",
    "\n",
    "4. Biological Graph Construction\n",
    "\n",
    "5. Cross-Modal Graph Attention Fusion (CM-GAF)\n",
    "\n",
    "6. Temporal Graph Neural Network (TGNN)\n",
    "\n",
    "7. Prediction Head\n",
    "\n",
    "The following cell initializes the complete PIDGN-T model.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# Initialize PIDGN-T Model\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "model = PIDGNT(\n",
    "\n",
    "    snp_dim=500,\n",
    "\n",
    "    clinical_dim=20,\n",
    "\n",
    "    num_classes=2\n",
    "\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "model = model.to(device)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "print(model)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Model Verification\n",
    "\n",
    "The initialized model contains all proposed components of PIDGN-T.\n",
    "\n",
    "The next steps include:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Optimization configuration\n",
    "- Loss definition\n",
    "- Training execution\n",
    "- Model checkpoint generation\n"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
