 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 7. Loss Function Configuration\n",
    "\n",
    "PIDGN-T optimizes the model using a multi-component objective function designed to jointly improve prediction accuracy, multimodal consistency, temporal stability, and interpretability.\n",
    "\n",
    "The total optimization objective is defined as:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    L_{total}=L_{cls}+\\lambda_1L_{align}+\\lambda_2L_{temp}+\\lambda_3L_{attn}+\\lambda_4L_{reg}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where:\n",
    "\n",
    "- $L_{cls}$ represents the weighted classification loss.\n",
    "- $L_{align}$ represents the cross-modal alignment loss between genomic and brain embeddings.\n",
    "- $L_{temp}$ represents temporal smoothness regularization.\n",
    "- $L_{attn}$ represents attention sparsity regularization.\n",
    "- $L_{reg}$ represents L2 weight regularization.\n",
    "\n",
    "To handle class imbalance between Parkinson's disease and control subjects, weighted cross-entropy loss is applied.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# Loss Function Initialization\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "criterion = PIDGNLoss(\n",
    "\n",
    "    lambda_align=0.1,\n",
    "\n",
    "    lambda_temp=0.05,\n",
    "\n",
    "    lambda_attn=0.01,\n",
    "\n",
    "    lambda_reg=1e-5\n",
    "\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "print('PIDGN-T loss function initialized.')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Weighted Classification Loss\n",
    "\n",
    "The classification component uses weighted binary cross-entropy to reduce the influence of the majority class.\n",
    "\n",
    "The class weights are calculated using inverse frequency weighting:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    w_c=\\frac{N}{2N_c}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where:\n",
    "\n",
    "- $N$ is the total number of training samples.\n",
    "- $N_c$ is the number of samples belonging to class $c$.\n",
    "\n",
    "The weighting strategy improves balanced learning between PD and control groups.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# Class Weight Configuration\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "class_weights = torch.tensor(\n",
    "\n",
    "    [1.755, 0.699],\n",
    "\n",
    "    device=device\n",
    "\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Class weights:', class_weights)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 8. Optimizer Configuration\n",
    "\n",
    "PIDGN-T parameters are optimized using AdamW optimization with weight decay regularization.\n",
    "\n",
    "AdamW is selected because it provides stable convergence for deep neural architectures containing:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Graph neural network layers\n",
    "- Temporal recurrent modules\n",
    "- Multimodal fusion components\n",
    "\n",
    "The optimizer configuration follows the experimental settings described in the manuscript.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# Optimizer Initialization\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "optimizer = build_optimizer(\n",
    "\n",
    "    model,\n",
    "\n",
    "    learning_rate=1e-4,\n",
    "\n",
    "    weight_decay=1e-5\n",
    "\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Optimizer initialized.')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Learning Rate Scheduler\n",
    "\n",
    "A learning rate scheduler can optionally be applied to improve convergence stability during long training processes.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Optional learning rate scheduler\n",
    "\n",
    "scheduler = torch.optim.lr_scheduler.ReduceLROnPlateau(\n",
    "\n",
    "    optimizer,\n",
    "\n",
    "    mode='min',\n",
    "\n",
    "    patience=5,\n",
    "\n",
    "    factor=0.5\n",
    "\n",
    ")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 9. Training Loop\n",
    "\n",
    "The training procedure consists of the following steps:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Load multimodal patient batches.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Perform forward propagation through PIDGN-T.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. Compute the multi-component objective function.\n",
    "\n",
    "4. Update model parameters using AdamW.\n",
    "\n",
    "5. Evaluate validation performance after each epoch.\n",
    "\n",
    "The same procedure is repeated for multiple random seeds during final evaluation.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# Training Configuration\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "NUM_EPOCHS = 50\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "training_history = {\n",
    "\n",
    "    'train_loss': [],\n",
    "\n",
    "    'validation_loss': [],\n",
    "\n",
    "    'validation_auc': []\n",
    "\n",
    "}\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# PIDGN-T Training Execution\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "history = train_pidgn_t(\n",
    "\n",
    "    model,\n",
    "\n",
    "    train_loader,\n",
    "\n",
    "    validation_loader,\n",
    "\n",
    "    epochs=NUM_EPOCHS,\n",
    "\n",
    "    optimizer=optimizer,\n",
    "\n",
    "    criterion=criterion,\n",
    "\n",
    "    scheduler=scheduler,\n",
    "\n",
    "    device=device\n",
    "\n",
    ")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Training Output\n",
    "\n",
    "The training process generates:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Training loss curves\n",
    "- Validation performance metrics\n",
    "- Optimized model parameters\n",
    "\n",
    "The generated checkpoint can subsequently be evaluated using the scripts available in:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "evaluation/\n",
    "```\n"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
